Pruned from Common/ specifically:
    src/TimeTrace.cpp
        Optional profiling support. When LUAU_ENABLE_TIME_TRACE is enabled it opens and
        writes `trace.json`; that is a filesystem capability outside Mantle's WIT surface.
        The header remains because Parser.cpp and Compiler.cpp include it, but its macros
        compile to no-ops when time tracing is disabled (as it is here), so no implementation
        or file symbol is needed.

Pruned from Bytecode/ specifically, because BytecodeBuilder.{h,cpp} do not
transitively need them (verified by grepping their #includes) and they exist
only to serve upstream's CLI dump/analysis tools this vendoring never builds:
    include/Luau/BytecodeCallInliner.h, BytecodeDump.h, BytecodeGraph.h,
        BytecodeOps.h, BytecodeValidation.h, Sccp.h
    src/BytecodeDump.cpp, BytecodeGraph.cpp, BytecodeGraphParser.h,
        BytecodeGraphSerializer.h, Sccp.cpp
This is a stronger exclusion than the usual "leave it out of the .Build.cs":
UnrealBuildTool compiles every .cpp/.c it finds anywhere under a module's own
directory tree, with no per-file exclusion list in ModuleRules, so a file
merely "not referenced" is still auto-discovered and built. The only reliable
way to keep an unwanted translation unit out is to not have it in the tree at
all -- the same reasoning CodeGen's full removal below already applies.

Pruned entirely, not vendored (see MantleCore.uplugin ticket T4.8 for rationale):
    CodeGen/    the native code generator (JIT). Never needed and never compiled;
                pruned from the tree rather than merely excluded from the .Build.cs,
                so the symbols do not exist in the repository to be picked up by a
                future glob or a careless "just add the whole folder" edit.
    CLI/        the luau/luau-compile/luau-bytecode/luau-reduce command-line tools.
    Analysis/   luau-analyze's type checker -- not needed to run scripts.
    Config/     .luaurc config file parsing for the analysis/CLI tools above.
    Require/    the CLI's require()-from-disk implementation -- filesystem access,
                exactly the kind of OS-facing code this vendoring must not carry.
    Inliner/    a CodeGen-only optimisation pass.
    tests/      upstream's own unit test suite (needs doctest, GTest-style).
    bench/      microbenchmarks.
    fuzz/       fuzzing harnesses.
    extern/     third-party deps of the CLI/REPL only (isocline line editor, doctest).
    tools/      misc offline tooling.
    .github/, .clang-format, .editorconfig, CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json,
    Sources.cmake, Makefile, CONTRIBUTING.md, README.md, SECURITY.md, .git/
                build/CI/doc plumbing for upstream's own CMake build, superseded
                here by LuauLib.Build.cs.

Compiled by LuauLib.Build.cs (see that file for the full reasoning). UBT
auto-discovers every .cpp under the module directory, so this list is simply
everything left in upstream/ after the pruning above -- there is nothing left
in the tree that is NOT meant to be compiled:
    Common/src/BytecodeWire.cpp
    Common/src/StringUtils.cpp             (TimeTrace.cpp deliberately absent; see above)
    Ast/src/*.cpp
    Bytecode/src/BytecodeBuilder.cpp   (the only Bytecode/src file vendored)
    Compiler/src/*.cpp
    VM/src/*.cpp                       (Luau's VM ships no io library and a
                                        deliberately restricted os library with no
                                        os.execute/os.remove/os.getenv -- there is
                                        no OS-facing translation unit to exclude
                                        inside VM/src the way quickjs-libc.c must be
                                        excluded from QuickJS)

Never compiled, and not vendored, for the reasons above:
    CodeGen (JIT), CLI, REPL, luau-analyze, Require (filesystem), tests, benchmarks.

